    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.deps\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nAfter updating mini.deps, this issue occurred:\n\n```\n(mini.deps) Error in `mini.extra` during installing plugin\nERROR CODE 1\nPROCESS REACHED TIMEOUT.\n```\n\nI found that the change introduced in https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/e7538b549361c9ac8416a07b0223ce03c508bfe7 caused mini.deps to stop respecting my proxy settings\n\n> i have:\n> ```\n> export http_proxy=\"http://127.0.0.1:8889/\"\n> export https_proxy=$http_proxy\n> export all_proxy=$http_proxy\n> export no_proxy=\"localhost, 127.0.0.1, ::1\"\n> ```\n> in my .zshrc\n\n\n.\n.\n.\n\nI’m certain that this line: `local env = vim.fn.environ()` produces a table env that contains my settings:\n\n<img width=\"480\" height=\"143\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/73e003fc-f9b5-4a27-aa7a-23d355ecb82e\" />\n\nbut:\n\n\n\nThis doesn’t work:\n```\nlocal spawn_opts = { args = args, cwd = cwd, env = env, clear_env = true, stdio = { nil, stdout, stderr } }\n```\n\nThis doesn’t work:\n```\nlocal spawn_opts = { args = args, cwd = cwd, env = env, clear_env = false, stdio = { nil, stdout, stderr } }\n```\n\nThis doesn’t work:\n```\nlocal spawn_opts = { args = args, cwd = cwd, env = env, stdio = { nil, stdout, stderr } }\n```\n\nonly this works:\n```\nlocal spawn_opts = { args = args, cwd = cwd, stdio = { nil, stdout, stderr } }\n```\n\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n```lua\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nlocal clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\nrequire('mini.deps').setup()\n\n-- Add extra setup steps needed to reproduce the behavior\n-- Use `MiniDeps.add('user/repo')` to install another plugin from GitHub\nMiniDeps.add('nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter')\n\n```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n4. error\n\n```\n(mini.deps) Error in `nvim-treesitter` during installing plugin\nERROR CODE 1\nPROCESS REACHED TIMEOUT.\nPress ENTER or type command to continue\n```\n",
