            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI can not reproduce exactly (since I don't use proxy), but I am 99% sure that this is indeed an issue with 'mini.deps'. Turns out, in `vim.uv.spawn` the `env` option should be not a name-value map but a `\"name=value\"` string array. I confused this with how `vim.system` does it (which 'mini.deps' can't use yet since it needs to support Neovim=0.9 :( ).\n\nCould you please check if the following patch fixes things for you:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/deps.lua b/lua/mini/deps.lua\nindex 9ee5b415..a1d3ac36 100644\n--- a/lua/mini/deps.lua\n+++ b/lua/mini/deps.lua\n@@ -1491,10 +1491,14 @@ H.cli_run = function(jobs)\n     local process, stdout, stderr = nil, vim.loop.new_pipe(), vim.loop.new_pipe()\n \n     -- - Unset special `GIT_xxx` variables that can affect `git` commands\n-    local env = vim.fn.environ()\n-    env.GIT_DIR, env.GIT_WORK_TREE = nil, nil\n+    local env_map = vim.fn.environ()\n+    env_map.GIT_DIR, env_map.GIT_WORK_TREE = nil, nil\n+    local env = {}\n+    for k, v in pairs(env_map) do\n+      table.insert(env, k .. '=' .. tostring(v))\n+    end\n \n-    local spawn_opts = { args = args, cwd = cwd, env = env, clear_env = true, stdio = { nil, stdout, stderr } }\n+    local spawn_opts = { args = args, cwd = cwd, env = env, stdio = { nil, stdout, stderr } }\n \n     local on_exit = function(code)\n       -- Process only not already closing job\n```",
